Simple crossword game for the reMarkable tablet: write letters in the squares with the pen.

Uses CWC¹ for generating crosswords, and a simple neural net using dlib² for recognising characters.

¹: http://cwordc.sourceforge.net/
²: http://dlib.net/


Running on the tablet
---------------------

reCrossable is an AppLoad³ application, for reMarkable OS 3.x with xovi and
AppLoad installed. It's made of:

  - ui/main.qml: the frontend, loaded by AppLoad inside xochitl
  - backend/: the backend process, which generates crosswords and recognizes
    letters, talking to the frontend over AppLoad's socket

³: https://github.com/asivery/rm-appload


Word lists
----------

wordlists/ has one clue list per difficulty, built from the xd crossword
corpus⁴ by tools/build_wordlists.py. Difficulty is approximated by
publication: Easy comes from USA Today and Universal, Normal from the LA Times,
Newsday and CrosSynergy, Hard from the New York Times and the Wall Street
Journal.

⁴: https://xd.saul.pw/data/


Building
--------

The backend is built with CMake. dlib is downloaded and compiled in, unless
DLIB_SOURCE_DIR points to an extracted dlib source tree.

For the Paper Pro family, with the toltec toolchain image:

    docker run --rm -v $PWD:/src -w /src ghcr.io/toltec-dev/base:v4.0 bash -c '
        apt-get update && apt-get install -y qt6-base-dev-tools
        . /opt/x-tools/switch-aarch64.sh
        cmake -B build -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=/usr/share/cmake/$CHOST.cmake
        cmake --build build
        cmake --install build --prefix dist/recrossable'

Then copy dist/recrossable to /home/root/xovi/exthome/appload/ on the tablet
and reload AppLoad.


Developing on a PC
------------------

shell.nix has everything needed. The backend can generate a puzzle on its own:

    cmake -B build-pc -G Ninja && cmake --build build-pc
    cmake --install build-pc --prefix dist-pc/recrossable
    cd dist-pc/recrossable && ./backend/entry --generate ginsberg

The frontend can be previewed and tested against a mock of AppLoad, which
serves dev/fixture-puzzle.json:

    QML_XHR_ALLOW_FILE_READ=1 qml -I dev/mock dev/preview.qml
    QML_XHR_ALLOW_FILE_READ=1 qmltestrunner -import dev/mock -input dev/tests
